    "created_at": "2025-01-24T04:29:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-24T04:29:41Z",
    "body": "Ah, I'd forgotten that's how it works. No, I wouldn't be in favor of conditionally adding properties to base `DOMException` instances. (I mean, it's not a terrible option, but it wouldn't be my preferred route).\n\nWhat about doing (1), but calling it `QuotaExceededError`, and retrofitting the existing specs to use the new subclass instead of the base type? It's hard to imagine this actually breaking anything, since it would still be a subclass of `DOMException` and the `.name` would still match.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/2611550011/reactions",
